# MQTT link to the ZUNEX station controllers (hardware integration).
# Leave ZUNEX_MQTT_URL unset to run on the mock hardware (demo/preview).
# Once the real broker exists, set these on the server (Replit secrets):
#
# ZUNEX_MQTT_URL=mqtts://broker.example.com:8883
# ZUNEX_MQTT_USERNAME=
# ZUNEX_MQTT_PASSWORD=
# ZUNEX_MQTT_CLIENT_ID=zunex-server-prod
# ZUNEX_MQTT_TOPIC_PREFIX=zunex
#
# Topic contract (see src/lib/server/mqtt.ts):
#   {prefix}/{stationId}/telemetry   station → server: port telemetry JSON
#   {prefix}/{stationId}/status      station → server: "online" | "offline" (also LWT)
#   {prefix}/{stationId}/cmd/start   server → station: { requestId, sessionId, minutes }
#   {prefix}/{stationId}/cmd/stop    server → station: { requestId, sessionId }
#   {prefix}/{stationId}/ack/start   station → server: { requestId, ok, code? }
#   {prefix}/{stationId}/ack/stop    station → server: { requestId, ok, code? }

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Security tokens (production only)
#
# This is a DEMO build (mock payments + mock hardware), so the demo panel
# endpoints (force-payment, fast-forward, abort) and demo scenarios work in
# production whenever the client is in demo mode (it sends x-zunex-demo);
# requests stay rate-limited. Optional hardening for a real deployment:
#  - ZUNEX_DEMO_TOKEN set  → demo additionally requires a matching
#    `x-zunex-demo-token` header (client: NEXT_PUBLIC_ZUNEX_DEMO_TOKEN).
#  - ZUNEX_DEMO_ENABLED=0   → demo fully disabled in production.
#
# Admin/telemetry endpoints always require `x-zunex-admin-token` to match
# ZUNEX_ADMIN_TOKEN in production. Falls back to ZUNEX_DEMO_TOKEN if not set.
#
# ZUNEX_DEMO_TOKEN=replace-with-a-long-random-string
# ZUNEX_ADMIN_TOKEN=replace-with-a-different-long-random-string
# ZUNEX_DEMO_ENABLED=0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
